/-!
# Dimension-Zero Geometry of Spec ℤ

Umbrella for the positivity theory at the dimension-zero point of the Tate family of a window:
descent of domination and its collapse to Weil positivity; the second-jet constraint on null tests;
the Tate twist as the shifted pair and as a tilt of the jump measure (real dimension: negative on
every window in large dimension, positive on short windows in small dimension), as a unitary
modulation (imaginary dimension); the sign change of the Jordan family at `k = 0`, the wall as a
Dirichlet inversion, the centred family as an odd exponential, and the failure of Tate positivity to
descend; the archimedean Tate cocycle and the unimodularity of the completed family on the critical
line; the Tate flow equation generating the jet tower from Weil's operator; Hecke similitudes of a
window; the archimedean place alone and the finite-level Weil cones; the ground-state
representation of a stage; zero modes as the radical and the Tate twists at an edge.
See `DimensionZeroGeometryOfSpecZ/README.md`.
-/
